        > QC automates and runs the approved tests from the test plan page (TESTCASES-&lt;KEY&gt;.md) with the PRD page (PRD-&lt;KEY&gt;.md) in its files … against the Dev branch &lt;KEY&gt; (its pull request is not merged yet); do not redesign them.

        *AGENTFLOW.md › QC (LeaveDesk)*

        > /qa-run · &lt;KEY&gt; [fresh | rerun | report] · write · needs testcases · produces results · push · attach RESULTS-*.md, evidence-*/*.png: Run the designed tests of a ticket on its Dev branch (or main once merged); AgentFlow pushes the results, the orchestrator opens the pull request.

        *Rules › Roles*

        > QC: designs the test plan; separately, automates and runs the approved test plan and reports each test round with evidence screenshots.

        *Platform*

        > task_run is checked before dispatch: /qa-run is declared in the agent’s AGENTFLOW.md, its mode allows writing, its needs are met.

        → Agent selection (H2)
      '''
    }
    agentflow.orchestrator.turn -> jira 'reply: QC is testing' {
      notes '''
        **Why this step**

        *Built-in prompt*

        > Be brief and concrete; say what you are doing when work will take a while.

        → Conversations (H3)
      '''
    }
  }

