        > When the ticket moves back to a status whose work was already done in this case, start NOTHING on your own. Comment what that status already produced (pages, pull request, last results) and ask what to change.

        → Status logic (H6)
      '''
    }
    admin -> jira 'replies: fix D-1'
    agentflow.orchestrator.turn -> agentflow.agents.devAgent 'resumes the task that did the work, with the instruction' {
      notes '''
        **Why this step**

        *Rules › Coming back to a status*

        > Start the work only when a person says what to do in a comment (e.g. “fix D-1”), then resume the task that did that work with their instruction.

        *AGENTFLOW.md › Dev (LeaveDesk, An)*

        > /executing-plans · &lt;ticket-key&gt; · write · needs approved-plan · produces code · push · attach pr-body-*.md: Implement an approved plan with TDD, commit, push and open the PR.

        → Resume the right work (H5)
      '''
    }
    agentflow.orchestrator.turn -> jira 'reply: the Dev Agent is fixing D-1' {
      notes '''
        **Why this step**

        *Built-in prompt*

        > Be brief and concrete; say what you are doing when work will take a while.

        → Conversations (H3)
      '''
    }
  }

